  "plan": "agentic-delivery",
  "section": "2.2",
  "description": "Every GitHub workflow of both repositories and what the cut (scripts/eng/delivery-cutover.sh apply, plan section 8.2 step 4) does with it: disable = its work runs on GitLab and the workflow is disabled in GitHub, the file stays; keep = it stays on GitHub unchanged. scripts/eng/github-workflows.test.mjs checks the list against .github/workflows on this tree and against the rules of plan section 2.2, so a new workflow cannot slip through unclassified. Fields: family (the row of plan section 2.2), gitlab (the template that takes over a disabled workflow, T1 to T7; none = dead), after_cut (where a kept workflow goes later), protected (a protected gate file: disabling it needs the owner command that names the plan), main_push (none = no push to main starts it; reads = a push to main starts it but it deploys nothing to production; frozen = its production deploy on push is frozen by cutover_gate; deploys-production = the one allowed exception), dispatch_only (only workflow_dispatch, repository_dispatch or workflow_call start it), pull_request (the two kept workflows that may run on a pull request).",
